  Sell it, or bundle it with anything sold.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
  The desktop and Android releases include the SDL3 runtime (zlib licence).
  The Windows build uses the MinGW-w64 runtime. Android also distributes
  the NDK's LLVM C++ shared runtime (libc++_shared.so).

  Graphics and image decoding: Khronos Vulkan and video headers (Apache-2.0
  or MIT, as specified per file), AMD FidelityFX SDK code (MIT), NVIDIA
  Optical Flow SDK declarations (NVIDIA redistribution terms), and stb_image
  (MIT). GPU features depend on the platform and available hardware.

  Audio and file decoding: ymfm by Aaron Giles (BSD-3-Clause), the ICE
  depacker ported from ym2149-rs (MIT), and dr_mp3 by David Reid (public
  domain or MIT-0), based on minimp3 (CC0). The LHA decoder's Huffman table
  construction follows Haruhiko Okumura's freely reusable ar002 routine.

  Cryptography: Monocypher (BSD-2-Clause or CC0).
  Fonts and glyph atlases: DejaVu (see its font notice), Open Sans (SIL
  Open Font License 1.1), and Permanent Marker by Font Diner (Apache-2.0).
  SemaDrive ambience uses wave recordings by jasinski, prepared by qubodup,
  and a rocket effect by Person (CC0). SemaTor also includes user-supplied
  floppy-drive recordings. The CC0 credit applies to the SemaDrive sounds.

  Component notices and credits are in Media/licenses on desktop and in
  licenses inside Android's assets/semator-app.zip. The Permanent Marker
  licence accompanies the SemaOS marker atlas.

GAME MEDIA AND ENHANCEMENTS
  Supply your own game disks or cartridges. SemaTor includes no commercial
  game disk or cartridge images. Xorg Unbound for Arkanoid II and the
  replacement artwork for Dungeon Master are available as separate
  optional add-ons.

